        data:
          "Nothing from outside the paper. The initial condition is the closed form $u(x,0) = U_0\\sin(2\\pi x/L_0)$ on $x \\in [-L_0/2, L_0/2]$ with Dirichlet conditions $u(-L_0/2,0) = u(L_0/2,0) = 0$, and the forcing is the closed form $f(x,t) = U_0\\exp(-(x - L_0/4)^2/(2(L_0/32)^2))\\cos(2\\pi t)$, a localized off-centre Gaussian with sinusoidal time dependence. The paper's footnote records that this forcing \"does not satisfy the general conditions for efficient implementation of our algorithm since it is not sparse\". The viscosity is set only through $\\mathrm{Re} = U_0L_0/\\nu = 20$; $U_0$ and $L_0$ are never given numerically, and the derived convergence parameter is $R = 43.59$.",
